      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory gave a practical, predictive framework for correlation-driven electronic phenomena in real materials.",
        "attribution": "These three researchers are central to the formulation, development, and broad establishment of the method.",
        "maturity": "It is a deeply established theoretical tool with extensive comparison to spectroscopy and material properties.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its collective and method-development history makes a three-person attribution necessarily selective."
        ]
